>-@

@-> *diaphane
@(grammata)
>-@

@@/ An embedded dialektos renders through its own tei exo; the
@@/ one that has one is bibliogramma, the bibliography. The rule
@@/ names it: a block of any other dialektos is no bibliography.
@-> *englossis bibliogramma
<listBibl>
@(grammata)
</listBibl>
>-@

@@/ A block of any other dialektos (a transcluded file comes in
@@/ as a block of this one) stands in the flow as it renders.
@-> *englossis
@(grammata)
>-@

@-> *diaphane-inline
@[<ref type="bibr" target="#@(cite)">]@@[<choice><orig>@(paradosis)</orig><reg>]@@(grammata)@[@(?paradosis)</reg></choice>]@@[@(?cite)</ref>]@
>-@
